(* P1. The server cannot tell which account paid for a chat.

   Two accounts (any number of pairs of them) each withdraw money into their wallets (the server sees which
   account asked, and the blinded message). Later two chats happen. On the
   left, A's money pays chat1 and B's pays chat2; on the right it is the other
   way round. ProVerif proves no server can tell the two worlds apart.

   `phase 1` is the line between stocking the wallet and chatting: the
   withdrawals are all over before the chats begin (see THREAT_MODEL.md,
   Timing: a withdrawal a second before a chat is not covered). *)

(* `!`: any number of such pairs of accounts at once, their steps interleaved in
   any order the server likes; each pair's devices talk to it over their own
   private wallet channels. *)
process
  ! ( new wa: channel; new wb: channel;
    new master_a: bitstring; new master_b: bitstring;
    (* each pair's accounts have their own names, which the server knows *)
    new acct_a: bitstring; new acct_b: bitstring; out(c, (acct_a, acct_b));
    ( Withdraw(acct_a, master_a, wa)
    | Withdraw(acct_b, master_b, wb)
    | in(wa, (sa: bitstring, ma: bitstring, va: bitstring));
      in(wb, (sb: bitstring, mb: bitstring, vb: bitstring));
      phase 1;
      ( Chat(choice[sa, sb], choice[ma, mb], choice[va, vb], minute1, chat1)
      | Chat(choice[sb, sa], choice[mb, ma], choice[vb, va], minute1, chat2) ) ) )
